From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: puffin <noreply@tlspuffin>
Date: Sat, 6 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] server: null connectionContext after deleteServerSecureChannel
 (fix use-after-free)

In serverNetworkCallbackLocked, when a connection attached to a SecureChannel is
CLOSING, deleteServerSecureChannel(bpm, channel) UA_free()s the channel object but
leaves *connectionContext pointing at the freed channel. A subsequent callback on
the same connection id then dereferences that dangling pointer -- either another
CLOSING (-> deleteServerSecureChannel on freed memory) or a receive
(-> UA_SecureChannel_loadBuffer on freed memory) -- a heap-use-after-free.

Under fuzzing the in-process event loop can deliver such follow-up callbacks, so
this UAF fires routinely and, because it happens during crash-handling/teardown,
double-faults LibAFL's restart (killing the whole campaign). Null the context after
the delete so any later callback takes the `*connectionContext == NULL` early-return
(the "closing without being registered -> ignore" path) instead of touching freed
memory. Mirrors the existing `*connectionContext = NULL` on the createSecureChannel
failure path in the same function.
---
 src/server/ua_server_binary.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/server/ua_server_binary.c b/src/server/ua_server_binary.c
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/src/server/ua_server_binary.c
+++ b/src/server/ua_server_binary.c
@@ -798,6 +798,9 @@ serverNetworkCallbackLocked(UA_ConnectionManager *cm, uintptr_t connectionId,
         } else {
             /* A connection attached to a SecureChannel is closing. This is the
              * only place where deleteSecureChannel must be used. */
             deleteServerSecureChannel(bpm, channel);
+            /* The channel is now freed. Clear the dangling context so a later
+             * callback on this connection id does not use-after-free it. */
+            *connectionContext = NULL;
         }

         /* Set BinaryProtocolManager to STOPPED if it is STOPPING and the last
